rustgis-grass-plugin (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * First package. Five GRASS vector modules as RustGIS geoprocessing tools,
    with every form read from the installed GRASS rather than kept by hand.
  * Three raster modules as commands with a panel: slope, aspect and viewshed.
    A plugin tool can take no raster and make no host request, so these export
    the chosen layer, run the module and add the GeoTIFF back, inside the two
    minutes RustGIS allows a command.
  * The computational region comes from RustGIS's Analysis Environment: its
    extent becomes the region's bounds, clipped to the raster and aligned to
    its grid, and its cell size the resolution, converted to the raster's own
    units. The panel can set the extent to the map view or clear it, and
    carries a cell size of its own that wins over both.
  * Each run reports the projection it worked in, the computational region it
    set and every distinct GRASS warning with a count. The region is never
    left at its default: a fresh project's one-cell region silently drops
    features.
  * rustgis-grass-setup generates the manifest from the GRASS on this machine
    and registers the plugin for the user who runs it.

 -- Yann Chemin <dr.yann.chemin@gmail.com>  Sun, 01 Nov 2026 13:55:00 +0100
